From: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 14:51:57 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: h713: describe the USB OTG controller

The DRD port's musb controller at 0x4100000 was missing; only the same
port's host side (ehci0/ohci0) was described. U-Boot drives it as a
peripheral for fastboot and is moving to this device tree, so describe
it: the D1/A33 musb glue, the OTG bus gate and reset, PHY 0, and the
interrupt from the stock udc-controller@4100000 node (SPI 32).

Disabled: Linux does not use the port's device side, so nothing changes
there.

Signed-off-by: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
@@ -1086,6 +1086,27 @@
 			};
 		};
 
+		/*
+		 * === USB OTG (DRD port, device side) ===
+		 * The musb controller on the DRD port; ehci0/ohci0 below are the same
+		 * port's host side. U-Boot uses it as a peripheral (fastboot); Linux
+		 * does not, so it is disabled here. Interrupt from the stock
+		 * udc-controller@4100000 node.
+		 */
+		usb_otg: usb@4100000 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun20i-d1-musb",
+				     "allwinner,sun8i-a33-musb";
+			reg = <0x04100000 0x400>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 32 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			interrupt-names = "mc";
+			clocks = <&ccu CLK_BUS_OTG0>;
+			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_OTG0>;
+			extcon = <&usbphy 0>;
+			phys = <&usbphy 0>;
+			phy-names = "usb";
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
 		/* === USB PHY === */
 		usbphy: phy@4100400 {
 			compatible = "allwinner,sun50i-h713-usb-phy";
